Z||000001||85Josh||04-03-2001||11:14 PM||||Different sized tires! Really, though, how fast are you going when it is this far off? Ten percent error is not unusual for a factory-new car, and if this error is at about 60 mph, that would be about right. BTW, the factory error is almost always optimistic!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||jch82||04-03-2001||11:35 PM||||It has the recommended tires for an '85.....215 60 14's. Is there any way to make it read the correct speed???<P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||85Josh||04-03-2001||11:44 PM||||Find a dealer with a friendly parts man (good luck!), or someone with a 22P parts book. I just won one on e-bay, or I'd look myself. What you need to find out is if they list different speedo driven gears. This is the gear that goes on the end of the VSS. If you can get different ones, you need to get one with fewer teeth to speed it up(if it reads slow) or more teeth to slow it down(if it reads fast). I'm not sure if these parts are actually available, so you might be stuck. Maybe someone else knows how to change the crystal on the speedo pcboard, but I think that would make for a pretty drastic change. Yeow, I just realized how long this post is! BTW, I really like your sig, cool quote (This from a country lover!)<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
